.TH "SPGEN-COMMAND_HANDLER" "1" "" "spgen 0.1.0" ""
.SH NAME
spgen\-command_handler \- Generates a command handler module and its test describe block
.SH SYNOPSIS
mix sp.gen.command_handler [options] <COMMAND>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Turns one command into the event(s) that fact happened.
.SH Prerequisite
.IP \[bu] 2
The Domain Model (../../../../domain\-model/README.md) contains the command and what it publishes.
.PP
The shape is identical for every operation — input command, output events — so this generator is fixed and takes no \-\-template.
.SH "What the generator does"
.IP \[bu] 2
The @behaviour Commanded.Commands.Handler, the aliases for command, aggregate and event, the @doc, the @spec (event.t() | [event.t()]) and the handle/2 head matching %Aggregate{} and %Command{}.
.IP \[bu] 2
The handler's dispatch … to: entry in the commanded router is contributed by the command (./command.md) generator, not here.
.SH "Left to you"
The body of handle/2, left as # implement logic here / # return events:
.IP \[bu] 2
Shallow — build the published event from the command's fields; the field lists are in the model, and this is the common case.
.IP \[bu] 2
Deep — guard, compute or derive before emitting; decided by the feature spec (docs/specs/), never copied from another citizen's handler.
.SH Tests
In the operation test (./operation\-test.md), under describe "Command Handler": the generator asserts the returned event type. The field\-by\-field mapping case and every branch a deep handler has are manual (Known gaps (../../README.md#known\-gaps)).
.SS "Generated files"
.IP \[bu] 2
services/api/lib/sportipedia/<_subdomain>/<composite>/<domain_object>/operations/<_operation>/handler.ex (handle/2 calling the aggregate)
.IP \[bu] 2
services/api/test/sportipedia/<_subdomain>/<composite>/<domain_object>/operations/<_operation>_test.exs (handle test asserting events)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-subdomain\fR \fI<SUBDOMAIN>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-composite\fR \fI<COMPOSITE>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-constituent\fR \fI<CONSTITUENT>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-model\fR \fI<MODEL>\fR
model root, default docs/domain\-model (relative to \-\-root)
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<ROOT>\fR
repo root, default inferred from the current directory
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
report the drift, write nothing
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR
FE: rewrite present generated units in place
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fICOMMAND\fR>
the element: esdm: reference, *.esdm.yaml, kind.name, or bare name
.SH "SEE ALSO"
spgen(1)
suites: operation, feature
